('Meta laid off 21,000 in 2022-2023, then announced its first dividend, roughly $3.9 million in shareholder returns per employee cut.','Meta\nlaid off 21,000','METADIV: first dividend $0.50/quarter ($2.00/year) announced 1 Feb 2024, about $5.1-5.3B/year, with an extra $50B buyback authorization. K02: $5.1B / 21,000 = ~$243,000 per cut employee; even adding the $50B buyback gives ~$2.6M. The $3.9M figure does not reproduce. The 11,000 + 10,000 = 21,000 layoff total is consistent with Meta announcements (analyst recall). "Tripled their stock price" is approximate.',['METADIV']),
