('Klarna AI handled 2.3M chats in its first month doing the work of 700 agents; headcount dropped 40%; IBM paused hiring for ~7,800 roles; Chegg fell from $115 to under $3 (97%).','Klarna\'s AI\nassistant handled 2.3 million','Klarna (Feb 2024 release), IBM (May 2023 Bloomberg interview) and Chegg figures consistent with reporting per analyst recall, not fetched. K02: (115-3)/115 = 97.4% (reproduces). Klarna\'s 700 were outsourced agents, not "700 people at Klarna" laid off.',[]),
('Marcus: $6,900 take-home; obligations $4,990; $1,910 left; $22,000 is about 3 months of expenses.','That\'s $4,990\nin committed monthly obligations','K02: 2,400+580+420+310+900+380 = 4,990; 6,900-4,990 = 1,910 (reproduce). 22,000/4,990 = 4.4 months of obligations; "about 3 months" fits total spending (~$6,100) better.',[]),
('Unemployment insurance pays roughly $4,200/month on a $115,000 salary.','unemployment insurance kicks in, roughly\n$4,200',f'Analyst assessment, not fetched: $4,200/month (~$970/week) exceeds the maximum weekly benefit in most states; only a few high-cap states (e.g. Massachusetts, Washington) approach it. Overstated for a typical reader. {U}',[]),
('COBRA raises the premium from $310 to $2,110; with a $340 prescription the monthly deficit is $2,900.','Your\nmonthly deficit is now $2,900','K02: 4,990-310+2,110+340-4,200 = $2,930/month (reproduces as ~$2,900). KFF 2025 family premium $26,993 x 1.02 / 12 = ~$2,294 COBRA, so $2,110 is plausible but slightly low for 2026.',['KFF2025']),
('Savings path: $16,200 after month two, $9,400 after month three, $8,000 gig, $6,200 at month five.','Month three, your savings are at $9,400','K02: at $2,930/month burn, savings are 19,070 / 16,140 / 13,210 after months 1-3; the $9,400 month-three figure and the $6,200 ending (vs ~$13,300+8,000-5,860 = ~$15,400) do not reconcile with the stated burn. Internal inconsistency.',[]),
