TITLE='Authentic title "Why Stable Jobs Are Financially Riskier Than Ever In 2026" is a contrarian "why X is riskier" reframe with a year stamp. The script delivers on it with a concentration-risk argument and a layoff burn-rate scenario. It performed TYPICAL against nearest-age peers that include the channel\'s large threshold hit "Why Everything Changes After Paying Off Your House" and "10 Unsexy Habits That Make Serious Money". Association only; no CTR or experiment evidence.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field, two-panel "EXPECTATION VS REALITY" layout in heavy black type. Left: a smiling cartoon man in a suit at a tidy desk with a green piggy bank overflowing with cash. Right: the same man disheveled, suit torn and stained, clutching his head, a cracked piggy bank and scattered bills. The image signals a corporate worker\'s financial collapse but does not reference jobs, layoffs or "stable" explicitly; the title carries that meaning. At 320x180 both headline words, "VS" and the facial expressions remain legible; desk details shrink.'
SCRIPT='A contrarian essay: two-neighbor cold open (laid-off salaried Daniel vs diversified freelancer Priya), decline of pensions and tenure, layoffs during record profits, concentration risk, AI exposure, a Marcus layoff burn-rate scenario, lifestyle lock-in, healthcare and vesting "handcuffs", behavioral explanations, and a call to build one outside income stream. Verified: BLS median tenure 3.9 years (lowest since 2002); KFF 2025 family premium ~$27,000 with ~$6,850 worker share; Meta first dividend $0.50/quarter. Wrong or non-reproducing: Meta "$3.9 million per cut employee" (~$243K from the dividend); mortgage share labelled take-home is actually gross; month-three and month-five savings do not reconcile with the stated $2,930 burn; $885 side income "three weeks of runway"; UI $4,200/month exceeds most state maximums. Several corporate and AI-exposure figures match known reports but were not fetched. The stored ending is complete.'
BEATS=['Cold open: Daniel laid off by email vs Priya losing one client.','COBRA cost and self-introduction with subscribe ask.','1980 pensions and tenure vs today.','At-will employment and layoffs during record profits (Meta, Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon).','Midnight-email layoff anecdote.','Concentration risk and diversification analogy.','Freelancer vs SVP income diversification.','AI invulnerability bias and exposure estimates.','Paralegal example; Klarna, IBM, Chegg.','Marcus layoff scenario months one to five.','Lifestyle lock-in and paycheck-to-paycheck survey.','Healthcare and 401(k) vesting handcuffs.','Loss aversion, Organization Man and sunk cost.','Income security: three streams, freelancing data, $885 side income.','Reassurance, one-question action item and close.']
